<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ghazi-ud-Din Haidar Shah</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 1769–1827</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ghazi-ud-Din Haidar was the ruler of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/awadh">Awadh</a> from 1814 and its first king, from 1819 until his death in 1827. Encouraged by the British, who wished to weaken the authority of the Mughal emperor, he renounced his allegiance to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/delhi">Delhi</a> and took the royal title. He built several monuments in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lucknow">Lucknow</a> and lent large sums to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-india-company">East India Company</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ghazi-ud-din-haidar-shah.jpg" alt="Ghazi-ud-Din Haidar Shah" width="203" height="256" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ghazi-ud-Din_Haider.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
